+## Time Machine Limits
+
+Search API and Context API requests with `snapshot_as_of` do not use the limits above. They have separate limits:
+
+| Tier | Search API (`POST /search`) | Context API (`POST /v1/context`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Tier 0 | 1 request per second | 1 request per second |
+| Tiers 1–5 | 50 requests in total | 50 requests in total |
+
+- A request uses 1 unit, also when it has more than one query or URL.
+- On Tiers 1–5, the limit is a total, not a rate.
+- Over the limit, the request fails with `429` and error type `request_rate_limit_exceeded`. After you use all 50 requests, retrying does not help.
+- Responses include the `x-ratelimit-limit`, `x-ratelimit-remaining`, `x-ratelimit-used`, and `x-ratelimit-reset` headers. Read `x-ratelimit-remaining` to see how many requests you have left.
+
